458	156,1037,442,1452	458. Upper part of the corolla of Stramonium (Fig. 177) in bud.	The top of a folded corolla in bud: the pleated limb twisted round on itself, the long tube below scored with fine lines.
459	170,1498,427,1761	459. Cross-section of the same, to show how it is plaited and folded.	A cross-section of the bud, the corolla's plaits appearing as five curved arms wound spirally round the centre like a pinwheel.
460	475,987,773,1619 - 700,1180,775,1470 - 612,1500,775,1622	460. Flower of Tobacco.	A long funnel-shaped flower with a five-pointed spreading limb, the stamens visible in the throat, a slender tube and a narrow toothed calyx at the base.
461	594,1507,843,1759 - 594,1507,607,1622	461. Its pod and calyx.	The pod of Tobacco held within its calyx, whose pointed lobes spread and curl outward around the rounded pod, with a short stalk below.
462	884,1514,1061,1758	462. Same, with the upper part cut away	The same pod with its top cut off, showing two cells packed with small seeds inside the spreading lobes of the calyx.
463	696,993,1311,1466 - 696,993,780,1165 - 1274,993,1312,1222 - 1052,1393,1092,1417	463. Flowers and berries of Bittersweet Nightshade.	A leafy branch bearing clusters of star-shaped flowers with swept-back lobes and buds on one side, and drooping oval berries on the other.
464	1274,1017,1571,1381 - 1274,1232,1312,1381 - 1418,1360,1456,1384	464. Flower of Henbane.	A broad open flower with five rounded, net-veined lobes, a darkly lined throat and the style at its centre, above a short calyx.
465	1257,1460,1478,1749	465. Pod of the same, opening by a lid.	An egg-shaped pod with its lid lifted back like a cap, the top of the pod full of small round seeds.
